{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Import Rule.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Import Rule.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css import rule css import rule","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Import Rule.md","fileName":"CSS Import Rule.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CSS Import Rule","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CSS Stylesheet Integration]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Stylesheet Integration","CSS Cascade and Inheritance","External Stylesheet Linking","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Import Rule.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Import Rule.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css import rule css import rule","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Import Rule.md","fileName":"CSS Import Rule.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CSS Import Rule","heading":"CSS Import Rule","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The CSS `@import` rule loads another stylesheet into the current stylesheet. Import rules must precede ordinary style rules, and they can include media conditions that determine when the imported rules participate.\n\nImports make a stylesheet modular, but the imported resource still enters the same [[CSS Cascade and Inheritance|cascade]]. An import is a CSS-level relationship, whereas [[External Stylesheet Linking]] is declared by the document markup.","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Stylesheet Integration","CSS Cascade and Inheritance","External Stylesheet Linking","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Import Rule.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Import Rule.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css import rule css import rule",